   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Pop-up Bike Lanes and Mobility Norms</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Pop-up Bike Lanes and Mobility Norms\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication of Study 3 with the original photos: four photomontages of the same tree-lined city road with a tram line, built by crossing two factors, a red pop-up bike lane or ordinary car lanes, with or without people using them (A: bike lane with cyclists, B: bike lane only, C: car lanes with cars, D: car lanes only). As in the paper, each participant first says how often they use a car as a driver, then reads a thought experiment (they have just moved to a new city and step out onto the street for the first time), sees one of the four photos drawn at random for at least 8 seconds, says what they would do on their first day in the new district, and rates how often the people living in this district use the car, the bicycle, public transport and walking for commuting, shopping and everyday trips, all on the paper's six-point frequency scale from 'almost never' to 'almost daily'. Rebuilt from Rollin & Bamberg (2021), It's All Up to My Fellow Citizens. Descriptive Norms as a Decisive Mediator in the Relationship Between Infrastructure and Mobility Behavior, Frontiers in Psychology 11: 610343, with the photos from its Figure 4 (photos: Michael Motyka) and the procedure and items from the Study 1-3 methods (CC BY 4.0). Image ids: photo_A to photo_D as in Figure 4; answers are in car_use, first_day (free text) and norms (item codes car_, bike_, pt_, walk_ followed by commute, shop or everyday; 1 = almost never to 6 = almost daily), the last two keyed by image id; the paper's group sizes and means are stored in the page's original-study block. Analysis as in the paper: average the three car items into a car-use descriptive norm and the nine bicycle, public transport and walking items into an eco-mobility descriptive norm, compare the four photos with one-way ANOVA and Tukey post hoc tests, correlate both norms with own car use, and code the first-day answers for mentions of cycling or driving. The paper (276 German online-panel participants in 2020, 65-71 per photo) found that both norms differed between the photos: the car-lane photos raised the car-use norm and the bike-lane photos raised the eco-mobility norm, the bike-lane photo with cyclists gave the highest eco-mobility norm, cycling was mentioned as a first-day activity only after the bike-lane photos, and own car use was not linked to the norms people read from the photos. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper ran in German with a commercial panel; here the survey is in English and anyone can take part; (2) the paper prints one example norm item ('The people living in my city district use the car for commuting'); the other eleven items are written by us from its four modes and three trip purposes, with 'this district' for the new district; (3) the paper's answer option 'less three times a week' is printed as 'less than three times a week'; (4) the paper does not say whether the photo stayed on screen during the questions; here it stays visible above them; (5) the paper does not print its demographic questions; only age and gender are asked; (6) the photos are the figure copies (about 360 x 360 px).\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"photos\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"car_use\",\n      \"title\": \"How often do you personally use a car as a driver?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Almost never\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"Less than once a month\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"Less than three times a month\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"Less than three times a week\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 5,\n        \"text\": \"Over three times a week\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 6,\n        \"text\": \"Almost daily\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"photo\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"comment\",\n      \"name\": \"first_day\",\n      \"title\": \"So you live here now. What are you doing on your first day in this new district?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"description\": \"Free text. Keyed by image id.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"matrix\",\n      \"name\": \"norms\",\n      \"title\": \"How often do the people living in this district do the following?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"rows\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"car_commute\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the car for commuting.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"car_shop\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the car for shopping.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"car_everyday\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the car for everyday trips.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"bike_commute\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the bicycle for commuting.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"bike_shop\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the bicycle for shopping.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"bike_everyday\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use the bicycle for everyday trips.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"pt_commute\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use public transport for commuting.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"pt_shop\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use public transport for shopping.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"pt_everyday\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district use public transport for everyday trips.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"walk_commute\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district walk for commuting.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"walk_shop\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district walk for shopping.\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"walk_everyday\",\n        \"text\": \"The people living in this district walk for everyday trips.\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"columns\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Almost never\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"Less than once a month\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"Less than three times a month\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"Less than three times a week\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 5,\n        \"text\": \"Over three times a week\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 6,\n        \"text\": \"Almost daily\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"1 = almost never to 6 = almost daily. Keyed by image id.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"gender\",\n      \"title\": \"Gender\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"female\",\n        \"text\": \"Female\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"male\",\n        \"text\": \"Male\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other or prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"age\",\n      \"title\": \"Age (years)\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"inputType\": \"number\",\n      \"min\": 18,\n      \"max\": 100\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"rb-original\">{\"source\": \"Rollin & Bamberg (2021) Frontiers in Psychology 11: 610343, Study 3\", \"n\": 276, \"images\": [\"photo_A\", \"photo_B\", \"photo_C\", \"photo_D\"], \"story\": \"We would like to conduct a thought experiment with you: Imagine you have to move spontaneously to a new city. You have rented the apartment online at short notice in order to find accommodation quickly. You do not know the district and the people who live there yet. Now you go out of your new apartment onto the street for the first time and the following picture awaits you. Please take your time to look at it calmly.\", \"button\": \"Next to the view out of the window of my new flat.\", \"minViewSeconds\": 8, \"photos\": {\"photo_A\": {\"lane\": \"pop-up bike lane\", \"behaviour\": true, \"n\": 65, \"carNorm\": 3.45, \"ecoNorm\": 3.82}, \"photo_B\": {\"lane\": \"pop-up bike lane\", \"behaviour\": false, \"n\": 70, \"carNorm\": 3.65, \"ecoNorm\": 3.64}, \"photo_C\": {\"lane\": \"car lanes\", \"behaviour\": true, \"n\": 70, \"carNorm\": 4.06, \"ecoNorm\": 3.39}, \"photo_D\": {\"lane\": \"car lanes\", \"behaviour\": false, \"n\": 71, \"carNorm\": 4.23, \"ecoNorm\": 3.18}}, \"indices\": {\"carNorm\": [\"car_commute\", \"car_shop\", \"car_everyday\"], \"ecoNorm\": [\"bike_commute\", \"bike_shop\", \"bike_everyday\", \"pt_commute\", \"pt_shop\", \"pt_everyday\", \"walk_commute\", \"walk_shop\", \"walk_everyday\"]}}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f1f2ef;--card:#fff;--ink:#1b1f1c;--muted:#59615b;--accent:#a33a2c;--line:#d9ddd8;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#f6e2de}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.08rem;margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:16px 18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.story{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;color:var(--ink)}\n.photo img{width:min(100%,560px);height:auto;display:block;margin:8px auto 0;border-radius:10px}\n.photo.small img{width:auto;height:min(28vh,240px);max-width:100%}\n.wait{text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;margin:10px 0}\n.it{padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.it:first-of-type{border-top:0}\n.it .st{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;font-size:.96rem}\n.it .o{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:4px}\n.it label{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;text-align:center;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:6px 4px;cursor:pointer;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.2;min-height:48px}\n.it label:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\n.it label input{display:none}\n@media (max-width:600px){.it .o{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:5px}.it label{min-height:40px;font-size:.84rem}}\n.it.miss .o,.q.miss{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:8px}\n.q{margin-top:16px}.q:first-child{margin-top:0}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer;font-size:.95rem}\ntextarea{font:inherit;width:100%;min-height:96px;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px}\ninput[type=number]{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;max-width:140px;margin-top:6px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Photos and questions: Rollin &amp; Bamberg (2021), Frontiers in Psychology 11: 610343, Figure 4 (photos: Michael Motyka) and methods (doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2020.610343, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='popup-lane-norms:state';\n  var ORIG=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('rb-original').textContent), IDS=ORIG.images;\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null, timer=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function fresh(){return {step:'intro',id:IDS[Math.floor(Math.random()*IDS.length)]};}\n  function chs(q){return (q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return typeof c==='string'?{value:c,text:c}:c;});}\n  function photo(small){return '<div class=\"photo'+(small?' small':'')+'\"><img alt=\"A city street seen from the pavement\" src=\"'+esc(files[st.id].url)+'\"></div>';}\n  function radios(n){var q=Q[n];return '<div class=\"q\" data-q=\"'+n+'\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+chs(q).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+n+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>';}\n  function pick(n){var x=app.querySelector('input[name='+n+']:checked');return x?x.value:null;}\n  function bad(n,m){var el=app.querySelector('[data-q='+n+']');el.classList.add('miss');el.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});err(m||('Please answer: '+Q[n].title));}\n  function intro(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>A new street, a new district</h1><p>This short study is about how people get around in cities. You will imagine moving to a new place, look at one photo of the street, and answer a few questions. It takes about 4 minutes.</p>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label></div><div class=\"card\">'+radios('car_use')+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Continue</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      var v=pick('car_use');if(v==null)return bad('car_use');\n      send([SPSite.answer('consent',true),SPSite.answer('car_use',Number(v))],this,function(){st.step='story';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function story(){\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"story\">'+esc(ORIG.story)+'</div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+esc(ORIG.button)+'</button></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){st.step='photo';save();route();};\n  }\n  function view(){\n    var left=ORIG.minViewSeconds;\n    app.innerHTML=photo(false)+'<p class=\"wait\" id=\"w\">Please look at the picture calmly. You can continue in '+left+' s.</p><div style=\"text-align:center\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\" disabled>Continue</button></div>';\n    var b=document.getElementById('go'),w=document.getElementById('w');\n    clearInterval(timer);timer=setInterval(function(){left--;if(left>0){w.textContent='Please look at the picture calmly. You can continue in '+left+' s.';return;}\n      clearInterval(timer);w.textContent='Take as long as you like.';b.disabled=false;},1000);\n    b.onclick=function(){st.step='questions';save();route();};\n  }\n  function questions(){\n    var q=Q.norms;\n    app.innerHTML=photo(true)+'<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"q\" data-q=\"first_day\"><b>'+esc(Q.first_day.title)+'</b><textarea id=\"fd\"></textarea></div></div>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><h2>'+esc(q.title)+'</h2>'+(q.rows||[]).map(function(r){var nm='n__'+r.value;\n      return '<div class=\"it\" data-n=\"'+nm+'\"><div class=\"st\">'+esc(r.text)+'</div><div class=\"o\">'+(q.columns||[]).map(function(c){return '<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+nm+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\">'+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div></div>';}).join('')+'</div>'+\n     '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Continue</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var fd=document.getElementById('fd').value.trim();if(!fd)return bad('first_day','Please write a few words about your first day.');\n      var out={},miss=[];(q.rows||[]).forEach(function(r){var nm='n__'+r.value,x=app.querySelector('input[name=\"'+nm+'\"]:checked');if(x)out[r.value]=Number(x.value);else miss.push(app.querySelector('.it[data-n=\"'+nm+'\"]'));});\n      if(miss.length){miss.forEach(function(el){el.classList.add('miss');});miss[0].scrollIntoView({block:'center'});return err('Please answer every line.');}\n      var sh={key:st.id,shown:[files[st.id].name]};\n      send([SPSite.answer('first_day',fd,sh),SPSite.answer('norms',out,sh)],this,function(){st.step='about';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\">'+radios('gender')+'<div class=\"q\" data-q=\"age\"><b>'+esc(Q.age.title)+'</b><br><input type=\"number\" inputmode=\"numeric\" id=\"age\" min=\"18\" max=\"100\"></div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Finish</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var g=pick('gender');if(g==null)return bad('gender');\n      var a=document.getElementById('age').value.trim(),x=Number(a);if(!a||!(x>=18&&x<=100)||Math.round(x)!==x)return bad('age','Please enter your age as a whole number between 18 and 100.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('gender',g),SPSite.answer('age',x)],this,function(){st.step='done';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  function clr(e){var r=e.target.closest&&(e.target.closest('.it')||e.target.closest('.q'));if(r){r.classList.remove('miss');if(!app.querySelector('.miss'))err('');}}\n  app.addEventListener('change',clr);app.addEventListener('input',clr);\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);clearInterval(timer);if(s==='story')return story();if(s==='photo')return view();if(s==='questions')return questions();if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','car_use','first_day','norms','gender','age'].forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{name:n};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('photos')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=IDS.filter(function(k){return !files[k];});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+esc(need.join(', '))+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"photos\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.id&&files[st.id])||a.consent!==true)st=fresh();\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
